# sprout

A watering reminder for house plants, as an offline-first PWA. Plain JavaScript modules, no
build step, no runtime dependencies.

## Where knowledge lives

| File | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `PRODUCT.md` | Who uses it, why, constraints, voice (impeccable's product record) |
| `DESIGN.md` (+ `.impeccable/design.json`) | Colours, type, components (impeccable's design record) |

## Rules

- Offline first: nothing may need a network connection or a server.
- No runtime dependencies without asking.
- Commit only when asked.
- Visual changes: take screenshots with `npm run shots` (needs the dev server) and look at
  them before saying a change is done; show them to the user.

## Layout

- `src/plants.js` — plants and their watering schedule (`dueIn`, `water`).
- `src/store.js` — plants in localStorage.
- `src/ui.js` — the plant list.
- `sw.js` — service worker: caches the app shell.
- `scripts/shots.mjs` — screenshots on an emulated phone into `shots/`.

## Commands

- `npm run dev` — static server on port 5173.
- `npm test` — unit tests (node:test).
